# Stack and conventions

Canonical product decisions live in `requirements-analysis.md`. Do not invent conflicting rules.

## Stack

- Backend: Django 5, DRF, PostgreSQL 16 (Docker Compose), SimpleJWT, drf-spectacular
- Frontend: React + Vite + TypeScript
- Auth: full-app JWT — every ticket/comment endpoint requires authentication

## Identity

- Custom user: `USERNAME_FIELD = "email"`; login with email + password
- Seeded users only — no registration, no user CRUD UI
- `created_by` always from `request.user`; ignore client-supplied values
- `role` is stored and returned; do not gate Core endpoints on role

## Architecture

- Business rules live in a **service layer**, not serializers or views
- Backend is the sole authority on validation and lifecycle; frontend must not be trusted to enforce either
- One consistent API error envelope for all errors (including DRF validation)
- OpenAPI from code (drf-spectacular), not hand-maintained docs

## Secrets and config

- No secrets in the repo. Read from environment with **no fallback defaults** — missing values fail loudly
- Provide `.env.example` with placeholder keys only

## Frontend auth tokens

- Access token in memory; refresh token in `localStorage`
- On 401: attempt one refresh + retry, then redirect to login

## Do not

- Commit `.env`, keys, or real credentials
- Hardcode transition allow-lists in the frontend (see ticket-lifecycle rule)
- Add ticket/comment delete (hard or soft) unless the brief changes
